r and the believers, let me strike his neck. He said. `ls he not one of the people of Badr? How do you know? Perhaps Allah looked upon them and said. “Do what you like, for Paradise is guaranteed for you.ʻʼ ʻUmarʻs eyes filled with tears and he said: Allah, may He be exalted, and His Messenger know best.";Musnad Ahmad 827, Book 5, Hadith 257;Sahih (Darussalam), al-Bukhari (3081) and Muslim (2494)](Darussalam);question #6;What role does trust in the Prophet's words play in the actions of his companions during this incident?
